What the Steel OS image contains
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Steel OS image is built on Bazzite, which is built on Fedora. The
software inside it keeps its own licences, including the GNU General Public
License for the Linux kernel and many other parts. Its source code is
available from:

* Fedora:  https://src.fedoraproject.org  (package sources)
* Bazzite: https://github.com/ublue-os/bazzite
* Steel OS: https://github.com/steel-and-code/steel-os

The Steel OS Portal app is yafti-gtk (https://github.com/ublue-os/yafti-gtk),
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3. The Steel OS build
changes its name, colour, icon and settings file; build_files/build.sh
section 16 lists every change.

Fedora is a trademark of Red Hat, Inc. Bazzite is a project of Universal
Blue. Steel OS is not affiliated with or endorsed by either. Steel OS uses
their names only to credit them.

Proprietary apps are not copied onto the Steel OS installer ISO. Where a
proprietary app is a default (for example Obsidian), it is downloaded from
Flathub after installation under its own licence.
